1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,900
Construction fleets: dozens of machines
across many sites

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,900
Machines get double-booked

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,900
Broken machines keep working
until someone notices

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,900
Site costs stay invisible
until the invoices arrive

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,900
Fleet Management: one place for equipment,
bookings, repairs and costs

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,900
Fleet manager: the whole fleet at a glance

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,900
Available, reserved, in service, defective

8
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:42,900
Two machines are overdue for service.
They can't be booked until serviced.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,900
The bell already flagged them

10
00:00:48,000 --> 00:01:04,900
A new excavator arrives:
CAT 323 joins the fleet

11
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:11,900
Site manager at North Ring Road
needs an excavator next week

12
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:21,900
Reserve equipment from the site page

13
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:31,900
First choice: the CAT 320

14
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:41,900
Conflict: it's booked until then.
The app shows the overlapping booking.

15
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:51,900
Free excavators of the same type
for exactly those dates

16
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:59,900
Including the new CAT 323.
One click sends the request.

17
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:07,900
Fleet manager: the approvals inbox

18
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:15,900
Approving re-checks the fleet

19
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:23,900
An older CAT 320 request now conflicts,
so it is rejected

20
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:31,900
The booking is on the central calendar,
next to maintenance

21
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:39,900
The site manager is notified right away

22
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:47,900
Operator: daily safety check before the shift

23
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:57,900
The loader's brakes fail.
That's a critical item.

24
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:07,900
The app warns: do not operate this machine

25
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:19,900
A critical defect is recorded
and the loader is blocked automatically

26
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:27,900
Mechanic: notified of the new defect

27
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:37,900
Plan the repair, then start it.
The loader is now in service.

28
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:51,900
Log parts and labour:
2 brake pad sets, 3 hours

29
00:03:52,000 --> 00:04:01,900
Total repair cost: 1.150 RON

30
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:14,900
Complete: the defect is resolved
and the loader is available again

31
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:22,900
Fleet manager: site costs against budget

32
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:32,900
Bookings and repairs are charged
to the site that had the machine

33
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:44,900
Pipera Business Park: 112% → 118%,
visible today, not at month end

34
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:51,900
No double bookings. Broken machines blocked.
Costs visible per site.

35
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:59,900
Next: user accounts with real permissions
and GPS tracking
